1️⃣ Signals vs RxJS — When to Use What?

✅ Architect-Level Answer:

Signals are Angular’s fine-grained reactivity model introduced to reduce unnecessary change detection cycles and simplify state handling.

🔹 Core Difference

Signals
RxJS
Synchronous
Asynchronous
Fine-grained reactivity
Stream-based event system
Simpler mental model
Powerful but complex
Great for UI state
Great for async workflows

🔹 When I Use Signals:
	•	Component-local state
	•	Derived state (computed)
	•	Reactive template binding
	•	Performance-critical UI

🔹 When I Use RxJS:
	•	HTTP calls
	•	WebSocket streams
	•	Complex async pipelines
	•	Cancellation logic (switchMap)
	•	Combining multiple event streams

🔹 Enterprise Strategy:
	•	Signals for UI state
	•	RxJS for async operations
	•	Keep streams at service layer
	•	Convert Observables → Signals in component if needed

That separation keeps code maintainable.

