2️⃣ Change Detection — OnPush Strategy

✅ Architect-Level Answer:

Angular default change detection runs on:
	•	Input change
	•	DOM event
	•	Timer
	•	Promise
	•	HTTP
	•	Any async event (zone.js)

This becomes expensive in large apps.

🔹 OnPush Strategy:

Component updates only when:
	•	Input reference changes
	•	Event originates inside component
	•	markForCheck() called
	•	Async pipe emits new value

🔹 Why OnPush in Enterprise?
	•	Prevents unnecessary tree traversal
	•	Enforces immutable patterns
	•	Improves scalability

🔹 Real Production Rule:

All components → OnPush
Except:
	•	Root app
	•	Rare dynamic container components

